1
00:01:29,464 --> 00:01:33,427
Three times nine is 27 . Four times nine is 36 .

2
00:01:56,908 --> 00:01:58,201
Come in , please .

3
00:02:02,039 --> 00:02:03,415
Here we are , Mary .

4
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:21,099
I have a most painful matter to discuss with you , Mary .

5
00:02:25,354 --> 00:02:26,730
Your sister .

6
00:02:26,897 --> 00:02:28,398
Have you heard from her lately ?

7
00:02:28,565 --> 00:02:31,443
No , Mrs. Lowood . She doesn 't write often .

8
00:02:31,610 --> 00:02:33,528
Have you any other relatives , Mary ?

9
00:02:33,695 --> 00:02:35,697
No . Jacqueline brought me up .

10
00:02:36,448 --> 00:02:38,784
Somehow , I never felt I needed other relatives .

11
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,702
That makes it all the more difficult .

12
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:41,787
Difficult ?

13
00:02:41,953 --> 00:02:43,455
Has anything happened to Jacqueline ?

14
00:02:43,622 --> 00:02:45,040
We don 't know , Mary .

15
00:02:45,207 --> 00:02:47,459
We 've been unable to get in touch with your sister .

16
00:02:48,168 --> 00:02:50,212
Sometimes she can be quite careless .

17
00:02:50,379 --> 00:02:51,588
Why don 't you try Mrs. Redi ?

18
00:02:51,755 --> 00:02:53,840
I have written repeatedly to Mrs. Redi .

19
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:57,010
She vouchsafes no information whatsoever .

20
00:02:58,261 --> 00:03:01,723
It is six months , Mary , since your tuition has been paid .

21
00:03:02,683 --> 00:03:06,520
Naturally , it 's impossible for you to stay on here as a paying pupil .

22
00:03:07,062 --> 00:03:07,979
Course .

23
00:03:08,146 --> 00:03:11,191
Miss Gilcrist and I have talked the matter over .

24
00:03:11,358 --> 00:03:13,944
You can stay on here and work

25
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:15,737
with the younger children

26
00:03:15,904 --> 00:03:17,447
as sort of an assistant teacher .

27
00:03:17,614 --> 00:03:19,825
But , Mrs. Lowood , I can 't just stay on here

28
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:22,119
without knowing what 's happened to my sister .

29
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:25,997
Maybe if I went to New York ... If I saw Mrs. Redi myself - -

30
00:03:26,164 --> 00:03:28,625
I doubt if you 'll get anything out of that woman .

31
00:03:28,792 --> 00:03:30,836
But if you 'd like to try ,

32
00:03:31,420 --> 00:03:33,964
I 'll advance you the money to make the trip to New York .

33
00:03:34,131 --> 00:03:38,260
Of course , my dear , if you don 't find your sister ,

34
00:03:38,427 --> 00:03:40,387
you can always come back here .

35
00:03:40,971 --> 00:03:41,972
Thank you .

36
00:03:49,187 --> 00:03:50,188
Mary .

37
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:52,649
Don 't come back .

38
00:03:53,650 --> 00:03:55,902
No matter if you never find your sister ,

39
00:03:56,069 --> 00:03:59,197
no matter what happens to you , don 't come back .

40
00:04:01,199 --> 00:04:03,618
My parents died when I was a pupil .

41
00:04:03,785 --> 00:04:07,205
I left , as you are leaving , but I didn 't have courage .

42
00:04:07,831 --> 00:04:10,417
One must have courage to really live in the world .

43
00:04:11,543 --> 00:04:12,753
I came back .

44
00:04:13,253 --> 00:04:14,463
Gilcrist !

45
00:04:30,562 --> 00:04:31,521
Agnes !

46
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:35,066
John Quincy Adams did not follow John Adams as president .

47
00:04:38,820 --> 00:04:42,240
Build thee more stately mansions , O my soul ,

48
00:04:42,407 --> 00:04:45,368
As the swift seasons roll ! Leave thy low-vaulted past !

49
00:04:46,828 --> 00:04:49,122
Let each new temple , nobler than the last ,

50
00:04:49,289 --> 00:04:51,833
Shut thee from heaven with a dome more vast ,

51
00:04:52,417 --> 00:04:54,544
Tilt thou at length art free ...

52
00:04:58,048 --> 00:04:59,090
That 's enough .

53
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,555
It seems all right , Joseph .

54
00:05:06,223 --> 00:05:09,226
You see , we do keep up the quality of La Sagesse products ,

55
00:05:09,392 --> 00:05:11,228
in spite of Jacqueline 's absence .

56
00:05:12,729 --> 00:05:16,566
But you must know someone who has seen or heard of my sister .

57
00:05:16,733 --> 00:05:17,901
I 'm afraid not .

58
00:05:21,613 --> 00:05:24,574
Your sister had many friends , but they were not my friends .

59
00:05:25,784 --> 00:05:27,786
I was only the manager of her plant .

60
00:05:32,415 --> 00:05:34,251
Mrs. Redi , there 's one thing .

61
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:37,045
With Jacqueline gone , how do you carry on the business ?

62
00:05:37,212 --> 00:05:38,588
What do you do with the receipts ?

63
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:40,090
How do you sign the checks ?

64
00:05:40,257 --> 00:05:41,925
Why , Mary , I 'm amazed .

65
00:05:42,509 --> 00:05:43,969
Didn 't Jacqueline tell you ?

66
00:05:44,553 --> 00:05:47,514
She sold the business to me at least eight months ago .

67
00:05:48,056 --> 00:05:49,683
It 's my business now .

68
00:05:49,850 --> 00:05:51,518
I didn 't know that .

69
00:05:51,685 --> 00:05:54,271
Yes , and I must say I 've done quite well with it .

70
00:05:54,437 --> 00:05:56,356
Perhaps even better than Jacqueline .

71
00:05:57,858 --> 00:06:00,193
There 's nothing you can think of ? Old letters ?

72
00:06:00,360 --> 00:06:04,072
Anything that might give me some hint as to where I might find Jacqueline ?

73
00:06:04,239 --> 00:06:07,158
Leave me your address . If I find anything , I 'll get in touch with you .

74
00:06:07,325 --> 00:06:08,618
I 'm stopping at the Chatsworth .

75
00:06:08,785 --> 00:06:09,703
Thank you , my dear .

76
00:06:12,998 --> 00:06:14,833
Why , Mary !

77
00:06:15,834 --> 00:06:18,295
- Hello , Frances . - How are you , honey ?

78
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:19,713
How 's Miss Jacqueline ?

79
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:22,215
I don 't know . That 's why I came to see Mrs. Redi .

80
00:06:22,382 --> 00:06:23,550
I 'm trying to find her .

81
00:06:24,134 --> 00:06:26,803
You mean she 's gone , and you don 't know where she is ?

82
00:06:27,596 --> 00:06:28,847
Come here a minute .

83
00:06:36,146 --> 00:06:38,106
I don 't get this .

84
00:06:38,273 --> 00:06:40,817
Miss Jacqueline 's so crazy about you .

85
00:06:40,984 --> 00:06:42,360
She was always talking about you ,

86
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:44,446
and she had your picture in her office , and ...

87
00:06:44,613 --> 00:06:45,572
I know .

88
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:48,909
For the first time , I 'm beginning to feel frightened .

89
00:06:49,075 --> 00:06:51,578
I almost feel as if I 'd never known my sister .

90
00:06:51,745 --> 00:06:53,038
Nothing 's happened to her .

91
00:06:53,204 --> 00:06:56,333
It 's just that I can 't understand her not keeping in touch with you .

92
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:57,959
I can 't understand it at all .

93
00:06:58,126 --> 00:06:59,461
Well , don 't worry about it .

94
00:06:59,628 --> 00:07:02,088
I saw Miss Jacqueline myself about a week ago

95
00:07:02,255 --> 00:07:04,424
at a restaurant the boyfriend took me to .

96
00:07:04,591 --> 00:07:08,094
A little Italian place down in the Village called the Dante .

97
00:07:08,261 --> 00:07:10,513
- The Dante ? - Yes , it 's on Perry Street .

98
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,682
Why don 't you ask the people who own the place ?

99
00:07:12,849 --> 00:07:14,643
They 'll remember Miss Jacqueline .

100
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:17,187
Anybody who ever sees her never forgets her .

101
00:07:17,354 --> 00:07:18,438
I 'll try there .

102
00:08:17,956 --> 00:08:21,668
I 'm sorry to bother you . I want to ask you about my sister .

103
00:08:21,835 --> 00:08:23,795
- Yes ? - I thought you might know her .

104
00:08:23,962 --> 00:08:25,714
She was seen here about a week ago .

105
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,674
Her name is Jacqueline Gibson .

106
00:08:28,258 --> 00:08:31,511
I don 't know no Gibson . This is a restaurant .

107
00:08:32,012 --> 00:08:33,263
Many people come here .

108
00:08:33,430 --> 00:08:34,931
She 's very beautiful .

109
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:38,101
I wish I could tell you what she looks like .

110
00:08:38,268 --> 00:08:39,936
I 'm sure you 'd remember her .

111
00:08:40,103 --> 00:08:42,272
She 's tall , with dark hair .

112
00:08:44,065 --> 00:08:46,276
Once you 'd seen my sister , you 'd never forget her .

113
00:08:46,985 --> 00:08:49,446
Giacomo , la bellissima madonna .

114
00:08:50,447 --> 00:08:51,281
Maybe .

115
00:08:52,032 --> 00:08:53,366
Let me look at you .

116
00:08:54,200 --> 00:08:55,702
Why , you could be her sister .

117
00:08:55,869 --> 00:08:58,496
Yes . Yes , if she made that much impression on you ,

118
00:08:58,663 --> 00:09:00,081
I 'm sure it was Jacqueline .

119
00:09:00,248 --> 00:09:02,333
She hasn 't been here for a long time .

120
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,544
- But she was here . - Oh , yes , yes .

121
00:09:04,711 --> 00:09:06,504
One day a beautiful car comes here .

122
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:09,591
This beautiful woman in furs gets out .

123
00:09:09,758 --> 00:09:12,469
There is a handsome man with her and the chauffeur .

124
00:09:13,136 --> 00:09:15,055
The lady rents one of our upstairs rooms ,

125
00:09:15,221 --> 00:09:17,974
and the chauffeur changes the lock on the doors .

126
00:09:18,141 --> 00:09:20,143
Then the lady does not come back .

127
00:09:20,310 --> 00:09:21,853
Not to live , anyhow .

128
00:09:22,020 --> 00:09:24,606
She came back three or four times ,

129
00:09:24,773 --> 00:09:26,566
but always alone .

130
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:27,734
Just to eat .

131
00:09:28,276 --> 00:09:29,736
You mean she just came here ,

132
00:09:29,903 --> 00:09:32,072
rented the room , locked it and left ?

133
00:09:32,238 --> 00:09:34,199
Yes . And pays the rent every month .

134
00:09:34,908 --> 00:09:36,993
Could you let me see that room ?

135
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:39,913
If it is hers , there might be something there

136
00:09:40,080 --> 00:09:41,915
to help me find my sister .

137
00:09:42,082 --> 00:09:46,586
No . The rent is paid . The lady asked us to promise .

138
00:09:47,378 --> 00:09:48,797
I won 't open the door .

139
00:09:48,963 --> 00:09:49,881
Please .

140
00:09:51,758 --> 00:09:53,301
It 's important .

141
00:10:15,657 --> 00:10:17,117
What did he say ?

142
00:10:17,283 --> 00:10:20,370
He said he always wanted to see the inside of this room anyway .

143
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:36,136
I tell you , young lady , when a thing like this comes up ,

144
00:10:36,302 --> 00:10:37,804
you 've got to go to the police .

145
00:10:37,971 --> 00:10:39,597
What do you think people pay taxes for ?

146
00:10:39,764 --> 00:10:41,891
It ain 't just to keep us chasing after crooks

147
00:10:42,058 --> 00:10:43,560
and regulating traffic .

148
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:45,770
We 're supposed to help everybody .

149
00:10:45,937 --> 00:10:48,565
Now , you 've got to go to the police about your sister , miss .

150
00:10:48,731 --> 00:10:52,068
Uh , I 've had some experience with the Bureau of Missing Persons - -

151
00:10:52,235 --> 00:10:54,112
Yeah . Well , Mr. Hoag ,

152
00:10:54,279 --> 00:10:57,157
lost persons are the concern of the Missing Persons Bureau .

153
00:10:57,824 --> 00:10:59,659
You stick to your poetry .

154
00:10:59,826 --> 00:11:01,202
You 're the poet , Jason .

155
00:11:01,369 --> 00:11:04,289
Well , in a way , that makes everything my business , doesn 't it ?

156
00:11:04,455 --> 00:11:06,416
Were you going to make a suggestion ?

157
00:11:06,583 --> 00:11:07,709
Yes .

158
00:11:07,876 --> 00:11:10,962
I was going to ask you to look into your own heart .

159
00:11:11,462 --> 00:11:13,173
Do you really want to find your sister ?

160
00:11:14,340 --> 00:11:16,718
Oh , my Jason , always laughing ,

161
00:11:16,885 --> 00:11:18,720
always joking to help others .

162
00:11:19,304 --> 00:11:22,432
He 's a good boy , miss . He just talks that way .

163
00:11:22,599 --> 00:11:25,435
I 'm a good boy , but no one listens to what I say .

164
00:11:25,602 --> 00:11:27,270
Now , you do what I tell you , young lady ,

165
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:29,981
and go to the Missing Persons Bureau for your sister .

166
00:11:30,523 --> 00:11:33,026
- If you 'll give me the address . - Certainly .

167
00:11:37,155 --> 00:11:40,575
- She was only 16 , and she seemed - - - Had she ever run away before ?

168
00:11:40,742 --> 00:11:42,702
What did he have on when last seen ?

169
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:44,787
He went out without his hat or his coat .

170
00:11:44,954 --> 00:11:46,915
It 's very cold for such an old man .

171
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:49,292
Any identifying marks or characteristics ?

172
00:11:49,459 --> 00:11:52,086
Scars , amputation , tattoo marks , speech impediments ?

173
00:11:52,253 --> 00:11:53,254
No , none .

174
00:11:54,631 --> 00:11:57,258
- Sign here . - Any further details ?

175
00:11:57,425 --> 00:11:59,427
Oh , she sold her business about eight months ago

176
00:11:59,594 --> 00:12:00,845
to Mrs. Esther Redi .

177
00:12:01,012 --> 00:12:03,348
What relation are you to the missing person ?

178
00:12:03,514 --> 00:12:04,432
Sister .

179
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:06,726
Sign here .

180
00:12:14,025 --> 00:12:17,695
Excuse me , uh , I 'm Irving August , private investigator .

181
00:12:17,862 --> 00:12:20,531
I think I can help you . Here 's my card .

182
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:25,036
The name may not mean anything to you , but just say the word ,

183
00:12:25,203 --> 00:12:27,372
and I 'll have your sister for you in 48 hours .

184
00:12:27,538 --> 00:12:28,456
Can you ?

185
00:12:28,623 --> 00:12:30,959
Look , sister , Manhattan is only nine miles long

186
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,585
and four and a half miles wide .

187
00:12:32,752 --> 00:12:34,003
I ain 't never been off it .

188
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,756
I know it like ... Like you know your own backyard .

189
00:12:36,923 --> 00:12:39,926
Now , you just get me a small retainer , say , uh , 50 bucks ,

190
00:12:40,093 --> 00:12:42,053
and I get your sister for you . I guarantee it .

191
00:12:42,595 --> 00:12:45,348
I haven 't any money right now , but I 'll get a job and - -

192
00:12:45,515 --> 00:12:47,517
Lady , this kind of work costs money .

193
00:12:47,684 --> 00:12:49,936
I gotta cover all the hospitals , the morgue .

194
00:12:50,103 --> 00:12:53,273
That 's the first place you gotta go , and it ain 't pleasant , the morgue .

195
00:12:58,361 --> 00:12:59,988
You know who I am , August ?

196
00:13:01,155 --> 00:13:02,031
Sure , I do .

197
00:13:02,198 --> 00:13:05,576
Then you know if I give you a little advice , it 'll be good advice .

198
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:07,328
Yeah , sure .

199
00:13:07,495 --> 00:13:10,039
That girl was looking for Jacqueline Gibson .

200
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:13,209
If I were you , I 'd forget it .

201
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:15,712
Okay , Mr. Radeau , it 's forgot .

202
00:13:21,926 --> 00:13:25,013
Hey , Danny , get me the file on Jacqueline Gibson , will you ?

203
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:48,953
- Whom do you wish to see ? - Mr. Gregory Ward , please .

204
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,663
And what is it about , Miss Gibson ?

205
00:13:50,830 --> 00:13:54,000
A personal matter . I was given Mr. Ward 's name .

206
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:56,169
May I ask who gave you his name ?

207
00:13:57,295 --> 00:13:58,296
The morgue .

208
00:14:00,590 --> 00:14:02,008
Do you feel all right ?

209
00:14:03,343 --> 00:14:06,471
I feel like an idiot , fainting in a stranger 's office .

210
00:14:08,264 --> 00:14:10,141
We 're not exactly strangers , Mary .

211
00:14:10,767 --> 00:14:14,395
Jacqueline spoke about you often . I suppose she told you about me ?

212
00:14:14,562 --> 00:14:15,980
No . At the morgue ,

213
00:14:16,147 --> 00:14:19,025
they told me a Mr. Gregory Ward had made inquiries about Jacqueline .

214
00:14:19,192 --> 00:14:21,235
At the morgue ? No wonder you fainted .

215
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:22,695
I wish you 'd come to me first .

216
00:14:22,862 --> 00:14:24,781
Then you know where Jacqueline is ?

217
00:14:25,239 --> 00:14:26,908
But I 'd give a great deal to know .

218
00:14:27,408 --> 00:14:28,368
Why ?

219
00:14:29,494 --> 00:14:32,872
I love your sister , Mary . I love her very much .

220
00:14:33,956 --> 00:14:35,958
It 's easy to understand now , isn 't it ?

221
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:39,295
A man would look for her anywhere , Mary .

222
00:14:39,462 --> 00:14:43,091
There 's something exciting and unforgettable about Jacqueline .

223
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:46,094
Something you never quite get hold of .

224
00:14:47,053 --> 00:14:50,431
Something that keeps a man following after her .

225
00:14:51,224 --> 00:14:53,935
Because I loved Jacqueline , I thought I knew her .

226
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:58,314
Today I found out such strange things .

227
00:14:58,481 --> 00:14:59,816
Frightening things .

228
00:15:00,775 --> 00:15:03,736
I saw a hangman 's noose that Jacqueline had hanging .

229
00:15:04,404 --> 00:15:05,238
Waiting .

230
00:15:05,822 --> 00:15:07,532
Well , at least I can explain that .

231
00:15:08,366 --> 00:15:10,660
Your sister had a feeling about life .

232
00:15:11,160 --> 00:15:13,871
That it wasn 't worth living unless one could end it .

233
00:15:14,038 --> 00:15:16,290
- I helped her get that room . - Weren 't you afraid ?

234
00:15:16,457 --> 00:15:18,292
Afraid she might commit suicide ?

235
00:15:19,293 --> 00:15:21,546
People who commit suicide don 't talk about it .

236
00:15:22,380 --> 00:15:25,007
No , that room made her happy

237
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,636
in some strange way I couldn 't understand .

238
00:15:29,971 --> 00:15:32,056
She lived in a world of her own fancy .

239
00:15:33,182 --> 00:15:35,101
She didn 't always tell the truth .

240
00:15:35,893 --> 00:15:39,063
In fact , I 'm afraid she didn 't know what the truth was .

241
00:15:39,939 --> 00:15:41,816
It 's difficult to explain to a youngster .

242
00:15:41,983 --> 00:15:44,527
I 'm not a youngster . I can understand .

243
00:15:44,694 --> 00:15:46,988
Oh . The color 's returning to your cheeks .

244
00:15:47,155 --> 00:15:49,365
You look as if you were coming back to life .

245
00:15:50,116 --> 00:15:52,785
Are you sure you didn 't faint because you were hungry ?

246
00:15:52,952 --> 00:15:54,787
You know , I didn 't have lunch .

247
00:15:55,955 --> 00:15:57,957
Well , it 's nearly 6 . Time for dinner .

248
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:02,920
Thank you . It was a lovely dinner .

249
00:16:03,087 --> 00:16:05,006
- Good . - But I feel guilty .

250
00:16:05,173 --> 00:16:07,008
It doesn 't seem right for me to enjoy myself

251
00:16:07,175 --> 00:16:08,551
with Jacqueline gone .

252
00:16:08,718 --> 00:16:11,679
Look here , you can 't make looking for Jacqueline your life 's work .

253
00:16:11,846 --> 00:16:13,764
You 've got to do other things . Live .

254
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:15,725
Get some enjoyment out of life .

255
00:16:15,892 --> 00:16:17,351
I hope you 'll let me help you .

256
00:16:17,518 --> 00:16:18,811
Thank you . Good night .

257
00:16:18,978 --> 00:16:20,021
Good night , Mary .

258
00:16:30,448 --> 00:16:32,950
Miss Gibson , I 've been waiting for you .

259
00:16:33,117 --> 00:16:35,495
I want you to know I decided to take your case .

260
00:16:35,661 --> 00:16:38,581
- Mr. August , I 'm not at all sure - - - Look , don 't say a word .

261
00:16:38,748 --> 00:16:39,999
I 've taken an interest in you ,

262
00:16:40,166 --> 00:16:42,043
and I 'm willing to put up my time to help you .

263
00:16:42,210 --> 00:16:44,295
Besides , I think I know where to find your sister .

264
00:16:44,462 --> 00:16:45,671
- Where ? - Wait a minute .

265
00:16:45,838 --> 00:16:47,048
This has got a lot of angles .

266
00:16:47,215 --> 00:16:50,593
You gotta take it easy . Tell me , do you know 3 Mrs. Redi ?

267
00:16:50,760 --> 00:16:52,595
Well , yeah . She bought my sister 's business .

268
00:16:52,762 --> 00:16:54,305
That 's what she told you .

269
00:16:54,472 --> 00:16:56,182
I looked it up in the Hall of Records .

270
00:16:56,349 --> 00:16:58,684
Your sister deeded her the business as an outright gift .

271
00:16:58,851 --> 00:17:00,811
Why would Mrs. Redi lie to me ?

272
00:17:01,646 --> 00:17:03,314
That 's what I tried to find out .

273
00:17:03,481 --> 00:17:05,483
I went to the La Sagesse .

274
00:17:05,650 --> 00:17:07,902
Used a phony health inspector 's badge .

275
00:17:08,069 --> 00:17:09,695
They let me go through the works .

276
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:12,490
All but one room . That room was locked .

277
00:17:14,325 --> 00:17:16,285
I 'd like to see the inside of that room .

278
00:17:16,452 --> 00:17:18,204
You think my sister is there ?

279
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:21,958
- Can 't tell . - Can we go there now ?

280
00:17:22,124 --> 00:17:24,293
Sister , you can 't just go breaking into places .

281
00:17:24,460 --> 00:17:26,629
They got a night watchman and locks on their door .

282
00:17:26,796 --> 00:17:27,964
If my sister 's in that room ,

283
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:30,424
it won 't make any difference about warrants and things .

284
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:32,510
- I want to go there . - I don 't know if ...

285
00:17:33,135 --> 00:17:34,720
If I wanna go with you or not .

286
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:21,392
Which room is it ?

287
00:18:22,727 --> 00:18:24,562
It 's the last door at the end of this hall .

288
00:18:34,572 --> 00:18:37,199
- You scared ? - Yes .

289
00:18:38,784 --> 00:18:41,120
- Let 's - - Let 's get out of here . - No .

290
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:47,585
You could go on , Mr. August . You could open the door .

291
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:49,253
I 'd stay right here .

292
00:18:50,713 --> 00:18:53,299
It 's only a little way , Mr. August .

293
00:18:56,302 --> 00:18:58,012
We can 't stand here all night .

294
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,389
You could go and open the door .

295
00:19:48,396 --> 00:19:50,481
Mr. August . The night watchman .

296
00:19:53,317 --> 00:19:55,569
The night watchman . He 's in the salon .

297
00:19:57,697 --> 00:19:59,657
Mr. August . What is it ?

298
00:20:00,157 --> 00:20:01,200
What 's the matter ?

299
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:05,162
Mr. August .

300
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:48,831
Do you know where you 're going , lady ?

301
00:20:49,582 --> 00:20:52,042
You 've been to the end of the line and back again .

302
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:53,669
I hope you enjoyed the ride .

303
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:16,252
Please . Please .

304
00:22:21,841 --> 00:22:23,425
I want your help , please .

305
00:22:25,469 --> 00:22:28,097
- Those men , don 't let them get out . - What 's the matter now ?

306
00:22:28,264 --> 00:22:30,599
- One of them has been murdered . - Murdered ?

307
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:35,729
What men ?

308
00:22:40,484 --> 00:22:41,735
But they were there .

309
00:22:42,528 --> 00:22:43,445
Oh , yeah ?

310
00:22:44,029 --> 00:22:47,283
Extra ! Murder , read all about it !

311
00:22:47,449 --> 00:22:50,327
Extra ! Murder , read all about it !

312
00:22:50,870 --> 00:22:53,914
Extra ! Murder , read all about it !

313
00:22:54,540 --> 00:22:57,543
Extra ! Murder , read all about it !

314
00:23:02,214 --> 00:23:03,173
Thank you .

315
00:23:16,103 --> 00:23:18,981
It 's about another murder . A woman on 52nd Street .

316
00:23:19,148 --> 00:23:20,608
But you do believe me ?

317
00:23:21,817 --> 00:23:25,404
Well , the important thing is the police won 't believe you .

318
00:23:25,571 --> 00:23:27,406
I saw him on the floor .

319
00:23:28,282 --> 00:23:30,784
He was cut ... here .

320
00:23:31,660 --> 00:23:33,454
The blood was running out .

321
00:23:34,038 --> 00:23:35,664
He was dead . I know it .

322
00:23:36,415 --> 00:23:38,500
And then on the subway , I saw him .

323
00:23:39,209 --> 00:23:42,421
White ... with the men holding him up between them .

324
00:23:42,588 --> 00:23:43,964
Yes , of course .

325
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:46,634
But the police would say you 'd probably had a bad dream .

326
00:23:46,800 --> 00:23:49,303
He was a kind little man , in his way .

327
00:23:50,095 --> 00:23:52,723
And I made him go down that hall into the darkness .

328
00:23:53,515 --> 00:23:54,975
I made him do it .

329
00:23:55,935 --> 00:23:56,936
Drink your milk .

330
00:23:58,312 --> 00:24:00,606
I don 't like to be ordered to do anything .

331
00:24:01,357 --> 00:24:02,524
I 'm sorry .

332
00:24:02,691 --> 00:24:04,735
I didn 't intend to treat you like a child .

333
00:24:04,902 --> 00:24:06,487
But you have treated me that way .

334
00:24:06,654 --> 00:24:09,323
I won 't do it again . We 're friends .

335
00:24:09,490 --> 00:24:11,784
I promise I 'll never order you about again .

336
00:24:15,371 --> 00:24:18,332
However , I won 't say that I 'll not take charge occasionally ,

337
00:24:18,499 --> 00:24:20,459
and I 'm going to take charge right now .

338
00:24:20,626 --> 00:24:22,378
- I have a job for you . - A job ?

339
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:25,339
Mm-hm . Remember you told me you were pretty good with youngsters ?

340
00:24:25,506 --> 00:24:28,509
Today I bumped into an old friend of mine , 3 Mrs. Wheeler .

341
00:24:28,676 --> 00:24:31,011
She runs a settlement house down in the Village ,

342
00:24:31,178 --> 00:24:33,347
and she 's looking for a kindergarten teacher .

343
00:24:33,514 --> 00:24:34,556
Why , I 'd like that .

344
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:37,184
It 's not much money , but it 'd be enough to live on .

345
00:24:37,351 --> 00:24:40,229
You 'd have to move out of that hotel and into a furnished room .

346
00:24:40,396 --> 00:24:42,898
Maybe the Romaris would have a room . They seem nice .

347
00:24:43,065 --> 00:24:45,025
- The people at the restaurant ? - Yes .

348
00:24:46,527 --> 00:24:49,863
If you want , I have time to take you to see Mrs. Wheeler right now .

349
00:24:51,532 --> 00:24:52,491
Yes , sir .

350
00:24:53,117 --> 00:24:55,119
Mr. Ward will see you in just a few minutes .

351
00:24:55,285 --> 00:24:57,162
- Won 't you wait , Dr. Judd ? - Thank you .

352
00:24:58,372 --> 00:24:59,915
Uh , Dr. Judd ?

353
00:25:00,082 --> 00:25:02,209
- Are you Dr. Louis Judd ? - Yes .

354
00:25:02,376 --> 00:25:05,462
I read your book , the one in which you wrote about the cure for drinking .

355
00:25:05,629 --> 00:25:07,631
You 're not a dipsomaniac at your age ?

356
00:25:08,048 --> 00:25:12,011
No , it 's ... It 's my father . I ...

357
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,762
I wanted to talk to you .

358
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:15,514
You wrote about cures .

359
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:17,766
I 'm sorry , I don 't practice anymore .

360
00:25:17,933 --> 00:25:20,185
I find it easier to write about mental illness

361
00:25:20,352 --> 00:25:22,396
and , uh , leave the cure of it to others .

362
00:25:24,982 --> 00:25:25,983
Yes , sir .

363
00:25:26,984 --> 00:25:28,527
Mr. Ward is free now , doctor .

364
00:25:29,486 --> 00:25:31,321
There are any number of other psychiatrists

365
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:32,781
who can help your father .

366
00:25:32,948 --> 00:25:34,950
Dipsomania is rather sordid .

367
00:25:35,909 --> 00:25:36,744
Thank you .

368
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:46,795
I 've come from Jacqueline . She needs money .

369
00:25:48,005 --> 00:25:50,257
I thought you told me you didn 't know where she was .

370
00:25:50,424 --> 00:25:52,676
I didn 't . She came to me a few days ago .

371
00:25:52,843 --> 00:25:54,762
To put it delicately ,

372
00:25:54,928 --> 00:25:57,598
her care imposes a financial burden upon me .

373
00:25:57,765 --> 00:25:59,808
She thought you might lighten that burden .

374
00:25:59,975 --> 00:26:02,561
If Jacqueline wants money from me , she can come to me herself .

375
00:26:02,728 --> 00:26:04,688
I 'm afraid she can 't do that , Ward .

376
00:26:04,855 --> 00:26:07,274
- It would endanger her . - This is nonsense .

377
00:26:07,441 --> 00:26:10,360
Unless I know where Jacqueline is and how she is ,

378
00:26:10,527 --> 00:26:12,321
I 'm not going to give you any money .

379
00:26:12,696 --> 00:26:14,156
You 're a curious man .

380
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:16,867
You 're willing to jeopardize Jacqueline 's life

381
00:26:17,034 --> 00:26:18,660
in order to satisfy your own curiosity .

382
00:26:19,119 --> 00:26:21,330
It 's not just for myself I 'm asking .

383
00:26:21,497 --> 00:26:23,791
Her sister 's here . The kid 's half crazy with anxiety .

384
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,251
As a man , you distrust me .

385
00:26:27,920 --> 00:26:30,005
Perhaps you can believe me as a physician .

386
00:26:30,589 --> 00:26:33,550
Well , then I can tell you that in addition to other dangers ,

387
00:26:33,717 --> 00:26:36,011
there 's a grave danger of Jacqueline losing her sanity .

388
00:26:36,470 --> 00:26:38,430
I would advise against you seeing her .

389
00:26:38,597 --> 00:26:39,556
But why ?

390
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:42,893
She 's been ill , erratic , but I 've never known of anything like that .

391
00:26:43,060 --> 00:26:45,062
You can believe me or not , just as you choose .

392
00:26:49,066 --> 00:26:51,777
- How much does she want ? - She can use a hundred dollars .

393
00:26:52,820 --> 00:26:55,322
- I 'll give you a check . - She can only use cash .

394
00:26:59,660 --> 00:27:01,370
I haven 't got that much in cash .

395
00:27:01,537 --> 00:27:02,579
How much have you ?

396
00:27:03,539 --> 00:27:04,748
About $ 45 .

397
00:27:04,915 --> 00:27:07,292
For the time being , I imagine that must do .

398
00:27:09,503 --> 00:27:10,504
Thank you .

399
00:27:11,255 --> 00:27:12,464
Tell me , how is Jacqueline ?

400
00:27:12,631 --> 00:27:14,174
- Oh , as beautiful as ever . - Tell me .

401
00:27:14,341 --> 00:27:16,260
She 's nervous , naturally , in the circumstances .

402
00:27:16,426 --> 00:27:17,636
What circumstances ?

403
00:27:19,596 --> 00:27:22,182
Mama , see ? Miss Gibson helped me .

404
00:27:22,349 --> 00:27:23,267
It 's a table .

405
00:27:23,433 --> 00:27:25,811
Beautiful ! We show it to Papa tonight .

406
00:27:25,978 --> 00:27:27,271
Did Michele eat her soup today ?

407
00:27:27,437 --> 00:27:28,814
She 's been an angel .

408
00:27:30,107 --> 00:27:31,483
Mommy , wait for me .

409
00:27:31,650 --> 00:27:33,026
Angelo , wait !

410
00:27:36,864 --> 00:27:39,992
Well , Mary , aren 't you the popular one . You 've a visitor again .

411
00:27:40,159 --> 00:27:42,327
- Mr. Ward ? - No , not this time .

412
00:27:42,494 --> 00:27:43,996
It 's a gentleman called Judd .

413
00:27:44,163 --> 00:27:45,038
Dr. Judd .

414
00:27:47,499 --> 00:27:48,584
Dr. Judd ?

415
00:27:48,750 --> 00:27:51,920
Yes , Miss Gibson . I 've come to take you to your sister .

416
00:27:52,838 --> 00:27:55,424
Don 't be so amazed . It 's a very ordinary matter .

417
00:27:55,591 --> 00:27:58,886
I 'm Jacqueline 's physician . Mr. Ward told me you were in town ,

418
00:27:59,052 --> 00:28:00,971
and Jacqueline sent me to bring you to her .

419
00:28:01,138 --> 00:28:02,764
Then you know where she is ?

420
00:28:02,931 --> 00:28:05,684
If I didn 't know where she was , could I take you to her ?

421
00:28:05,851 --> 00:28:08,061
Get your hat and coat . We haven 't much time .

422
00:28:13,984 --> 00:28:15,944
It 's amid marble splendors such as these

423
00:28:16,111 --> 00:28:17,321
that Jacqueline dwells .

424
00:28:18,155 --> 00:28:19,865
One can take either staircase .

425
00:28:20,032 --> 00:28:22,409
I prefer the left , the sinister side .

426
00:28:41,303 --> 00:28:42,846
She 's not here . She 's gone .

427
00:28:55,359 --> 00:28:57,069
I don 't know why she left .

428
00:28:57,236 --> 00:28:58,612
She knows she shouldn 't have .

429
00:29:10,374 --> 00:29:12,042
She 's left me to meet them alone .

430
00:29:12,751 --> 00:29:13,794
I can 't .

431
00:29:14,628 --> 00:29:16,922
What makes you so nervous , Dr. Judd ?

432
00:29:17,089 --> 00:29:19,174
- Who are they ? - I can 't stay here .

433
00:29:19,341 --> 00:29:20,425
I 'll have to leave you .

434
00:29:44,032 --> 00:29:45,117
Jacqueline !

435
00:30:58,398 --> 00:30:59,483
Is this her ?

436
00:31:00,484 --> 00:31:01,610
No .

437
00:31:04,738 --> 00:31:06,907
- Where 's Jacqueline Gibson ? - I don 't know .

438
00:31:07,074 --> 00:31:09,701
- She was just here . Where 'd she go ? - I tell you , I don 't know .

439
00:31:09,868 --> 00:31:11,787
That 's funny , you went out with her and came back alone

440
00:31:11,953 --> 00:31:14,164
- and don 't know where she went ? - I don 't know .

441
00:31:15,624 --> 00:31:17,376
Why do you want Jacqueline ?

442
00:31:17,542 --> 00:31:19,503
What right have you to question me ?

443
00:31:19,669 --> 00:31:21,129
I have all the right in the world .

444
00:31:21,296 --> 00:31:23,382
I 'm Paul Radeau , a private investigator ,

445
00:31:23,548 --> 00:31:25,926
and I 've been hired to find your sister by her husband ,

446
00:31:26,093 --> 00:31:27,594
Gregory Ward .

447
00:31:27,761 --> 00:31:28,762
Husband .

448
00:31:47,614 --> 00:31:49,908
Say , what are you thinking of , Bella ? Can I eat dry ?

449
00:31:50,075 --> 00:31:52,661
Oh , the wine . I have forgotten the wine .

450
00:31:56,123 --> 00:31:58,333
Look , Mary , just because I kept a secret from you

451
00:31:58,500 --> 00:31:59,918
doesn 't make a monster of me .

452
00:32:00,085 --> 00:32:02,462
Please . I can 't go on explaining things like this

453
00:32:02,629 --> 00:32:03,797
to your right ear .

454
00:32:03,964 --> 00:32:05,674
Last night in this very restaurant ,

455
00:32:05,841 --> 00:32:08,468
Mr. Jason Hoag paid a very pretty compliment to my right ear .

456
00:32:08,635 --> 00:32:10,512
- Who the devil is he ? - A poet .

457
00:32:10,679 --> 00:32:12,139
He 's sitting right over there .

458
00:32:12,305 --> 00:32:14,599
That 's his table , the one at the feet of Dante .

459
00:32:15,267 --> 00:32:17,561
Do you remember the first day you came to my office ,

460
00:32:17,727 --> 00:32:19,104
frightened and broken up ,

461
00:32:19,271 --> 00:32:21,940
and I asked you if Jacqueline had ever spoken about me to you ?

462
00:32:22,107 --> 00:32:23,275
You said no .

463
00:32:23,442 --> 00:32:25,735
Well , then how could I tell you we were married ?

464
00:32:25,902 --> 00:32:28,488
And afterwards ... Well , I didn 't tell you afterwards

465
00:32:28,655 --> 00:32:30,699
because there were so many things coming up

466
00:32:30,866 --> 00:32:33,076
to make me worry and wonder ...

467
00:32:33,660 --> 00:32:34,911
Ah , my beautiful one .

468
00:32:35,078 --> 00:32:37,789
Why do you bring me wine , when you yourself are so intoxicating ?

469
00:32:39,291 --> 00:32:41,084
You 're my favorite audience , Bella .

470
00:32:45,589 --> 00:32:48,133
Why can 't everyone be happy like we are ?

471
00:32:48,300 --> 00:32:50,051
Laugh and have a good time .

472
00:32:50,552 --> 00:32:51,678
That poor little one .

473
00:32:51,845 --> 00:32:54,514
So sad because she can 't find her sister .

474
00:32:54,681 --> 00:32:57,017
And that man with her , he doesn 't make her laugh .

475
00:32:57,184 --> 00:32:58,393
Just sits and talks .

476
00:32:58,935 --> 00:33:01,688
We are happy , Mrs. Romari , because you have everything ,

477
00:33:01,855 --> 00:33:03,690
and I have nothing to lose .

478
00:33:03,857 --> 00:33:05,775
Why , you should make her laugh , Jason .

479
00:33:05,942 --> 00:33:07,611
Come , make jokes for her .

480
00:33:07,777 --> 00:33:10,405
You could have told me anytime you were Jacqueline 's husband .

481
00:33:10,572 --> 00:33:11,948
Things change , Mary .

482
00:33:12,115 --> 00:33:14,451
The reasons for finding Jacqueline changed .

483
00:33:15,494 --> 00:33:17,412
I want to find her to settle things .

484
00:33:17,996 --> 00:33:20,081
What things ? Why ?

485
00:33:21,124 --> 00:33:22,876
Why you two are so sad ?

486
00:33:23,043 --> 00:33:26,004
Your food will not digest , and your wine will sour .

487
00:33:26,171 --> 00:33:27,464
You must laugh to eat well .

488
00:33:27,631 --> 00:33:29,674
I 've brought Jason to make you laugh .

489
00:33:30,217 --> 00:33:32,636
Um , Mr. Hoag , this is Mr. Ward .

490
00:33:36,348 --> 00:33:38,850
Sit down . I 'll get the rest of your dinner .

491
00:33:44,231 --> 00:33:46,316
I 'm under orders to make you laugh .

492
00:33:46,942 --> 00:33:48,318
In Mrs. Romari 's mind ,

493
00:33:48,485 --> 00:33:50,737
poetry and humor have some strange affinity ,

494
00:33:50,904 --> 00:33:52,447
which they don 't have in fact .

495
00:33:52,948 --> 00:33:54,658
She wants me to play the fool for you ,

496
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:58,245
but ... suddenly , Miss Gibson , I feel as sad as you do .

497
00:33:58,411 --> 00:34:00,455
Well , then , I 've spoiled your dinner .

498
00:34:00,622 --> 00:34:03,041
You food won 't digest , and your wine will sour .

499
00:34:03,208 --> 00:34:04,668
You 'll have to make all the jokes

500
00:34:04,834 --> 00:34:06,920
because I 'm going to be serious .

501
00:34:08,672 --> 00:34:10,382
I 'm going to find your sister .

502
00:34:11,716 --> 00:34:13,802
Shuffle the cards well , Natalie .

503
00:34:13,969 --> 00:34:16,179
This is a trick of telepathy , not card manipulation .

504
00:34:18,890 --> 00:34:20,433
Now pass the cards to me .

505
00:34:21,184 --> 00:34:24,145
Gladys , will you hand the cards to Louis while I answer the door ?

506
00:34:33,321 --> 00:34:34,906
Jason ! How nice to see you .

507
00:34:35,073 --> 00:34:36,575
I 've brought some friends , Natalie .

508
00:34:36,741 --> 00:34:39,411
- May we come to your party ? - Oh , of course . Come in .

509
00:34:39,578 --> 00:34:42,998
Now , all of you must remember the cards that you have selected ...

510
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:47,794
- Mrs. Cortez , Mary Gibson and Mr. Ward . - So nice to meet you .

511
00:34:47,961 --> 00:34:49,754
The cards can 't speak for themselves .

512
00:34:49,921 --> 00:34:52,507
- It 's purely a matter of the mind . - You 'll have to excuse me .

513
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:55,510
Mrs. Freeman , yours was the jack of spades .

514
00:34:55,677 --> 00:34:57,178
Gladys , seven of diamonds .

515
00:34:57,345 --> 00:34:59,014
Yours , Mrs. Gosden , the queen of hearts .

516
00:34:59,180 --> 00:35:00,890
How do you ever do it , Louis ?

517
00:35:01,808 --> 00:35:02,809
Hello , Jason .

518
00:35:05,353 --> 00:35:06,688
Where 's Jacqueline Gibson ?

519
00:35:07,981 --> 00:35:10,609
- What a peculiar question . - I saw you with her last week .

520
00:35:10,775 --> 00:35:12,819
I knew you 'd be here tonight . Where is she ?

521
00:35:12,986 --> 00:35:15,822
My dear fellow , it 's neither your business to ask , nor mine to tell .

522
00:35:15,989 --> 00:35:16,740
Oh , wait .

523
00:35:17,157 --> 00:35:18,199
Look over there .

524
00:35:18,908 --> 00:35:22,829
Do you see that girl ? That 's Jacqueline 's sister .

525
00:35:22,996 --> 00:35:24,748
It 's because of her that I ask .

526
00:35:24,914 --> 00:35:26,041
But why come to me ?

527
00:35:26,791 --> 00:35:28,918
Because there was another girl , years ago .

528
00:35:29,085 --> 00:35:30,253
A nice girl .

529
00:35:30,420 --> 00:35:31,963
She lived in Barrow Street .

530
00:35:32,631 --> 00:35:34,299
I saw her with you once .

531
00:35:34,466 --> 00:35:35,967
I saw her with you twice .

532
00:35:36,885 --> 00:35:38,386
And then I never saw her again .

533
00:35:38,553 --> 00:35:39,846
She was my patient .

534
00:35:41,222 --> 00:35:42,307
What was she to you ?

535
00:35:43,391 --> 00:35:45,727
I don 't think you 'd understand if I told you .

536
00:35:45,894 --> 00:35:48,021
I think I understand without your telling me .

537
00:35:48,688 --> 00:35:50,690
I know something of your history , Jason .

538
00:35:51,191 --> 00:35:53,401
I know you haven 't written for ten years .

539
00:35:54,235 --> 00:35:55,695
I 've lost the knack .

540
00:35:55,862 --> 00:35:57,447
After that wonderful first book ?

541
00:35:57,989 --> 00:36:00,700
After all the adulation and good reviews ?

542
00:36:02,243 --> 00:36:04,704
I 'd have given anything to have written that book .

543
00:36:06,873 --> 00:36:11,086
You had all my admiration and respect ... once .

544
00:36:13,672 --> 00:36:16,591
There you are . Do you know any more card tricks ?

545
00:36:20,095 --> 00:36:21,221
Hello , Ward .

546
00:36:22,222 --> 00:36:23,515
My dear Miss Gibson .

547
00:36:23,682 --> 00:36:24,599
Gibson ?

548
00:36:24,766 --> 00:36:26,267
Are you Jacqueline 's sister ?

549
00:36:26,434 --> 00:36:28,019
- Yes . Do you - - ? - Know her ?

550
00:36:28,186 --> 00:36:29,896
Oh , my dear , we were intimate .

551
00:36:30,063 --> 00:36:31,940
The times we used to have together .

552
00:36:32,107 --> 00:36:34,859
I 'll bet she never told you about that . You 're too young .

553
00:36:35,026 --> 00:36:38,488
I 'm afraid you don 't understand . Miss Gibson 's sister is missing .

554
00:36:38,655 --> 00:36:40,824
Missing ? Well , no wonder .

555
00:36:40,990 --> 00:36:42,450
When she took up with Louis Judd ,

556
00:36:42,617 --> 00:36:44,619
she went out of circulation just like that .

557
00:36:47,914 --> 00:36:50,083
My dear , have I said something ?

558
00:36:57,841 --> 00:36:59,259
Too many people here .

559
00:37:01,428 --> 00:37:03,388
Perhaps Jacqueline is lonely for me .

560
00:37:04,848 --> 00:37:07,517
You see , Mary , I 'm not quite a fool .

561
00:37:08,810 --> 00:37:10,687
At least you knew about Dr. Judd .

562
00:37:11,187 --> 00:37:12,272
Yes .

563
00:37:12,439 --> 00:37:13,732
And you knew he 'd be here .

564
00:37:14,315 --> 00:37:15,233
Yes .

565
00:37:16,067 --> 00:37:18,319
And now that I 've shown you that I know that much ,

566
00:37:18,486 --> 00:37:21,865
and can guess more , will you trust me to look for Jacqueline ?

567
00:37:22,949 --> 00:37:24,909
I want you to look for Jacqueline .

568
00:37:28,246 --> 00:37:30,081
I 'm a terrible failure , Mary .

569
00:37:30,874 --> 00:37:33,877
A book clerk by day and a poet by night .

570
00:37:34,544 --> 00:37:35,920
Not a very good one .

571
00:37:37,213 --> 00:37:40,175
But if you 'll trust me , at this one thing , I won 't fail .

572
00:37:40,800 --> 00:37:42,343
I 'll find your sister .

573
00:37:42,510 --> 00:37:44,679
You have such lovely hands , Miss Gottschalk .

574
00:37:44,846 --> 00:37:46,181
So slim and capable .

575
00:37:46,723 --> 00:37:49,017
Mr. Hoag , I really shouldn 't be doing this , you know .

576
00:37:49,184 --> 00:37:51,644
It 's against the rules . Why did you say you wanted them ?

577
00:37:51,811 --> 00:37:53,897
I 'd like to see what kind of books my friends read

578
00:37:54,063 --> 00:37:55,899
so I 'll know what to buy them as presents .

579
00:37:56,065 --> 00:37:57,817
Nothing nicer than a book for a gift .

580
00:37:57,984 --> 00:37:58,902
Hmm .

581
00:37:59,611 --> 00:38:01,446
Who was the first one ? Mrs. Redi ?

582
00:38:01,613 --> 00:38:03,740
- Mm-hm . - P , Q , R ...

583
00:38:05,074 --> 00:38:06,409
Yes . Here it is .

584
00:38:06,910 --> 00:38:10,079
- And the other was Judd ? - Yes , Dr. Louis Judd .

585
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:12,540
Mm-hm . He 's here too .

586
00:38:13,082 --> 00:38:15,251
Would it be asking too much , Miss Gottschalk ,

587
00:38:15,418 --> 00:38:16,669
for you to get me these books ?

588
00:38:16,836 --> 00:38:18,671
No , not at all , Mr. Hoag .

589
00:38:20,089 --> 00:38:21,341
Why , Mr. Hoag ,

590
00:38:21,508 --> 00:38:23,802
most of these books are on the closed shelf .

591
00:38:23,968 --> 00:38:25,261
You 'll have to get permission .

592
00:38:25,428 --> 00:38:28,473
I wouldn 't want to take them out . I 'd just like to look at them .

593
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:30,683
Well , since you 're over 21 .

594
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:35,104
Mimi .

595
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:40,151
Come in .

596
00:38:42,529 --> 00:38:43,738
What is it ?

597
00:38:43,905 --> 00:38:46,825
A parallelogram with a split triangle in its very center .

598
00:38:47,242 --> 00:38:50,870
I found out that Mrs. Redi reads the same books as Dr. Judd .

599
00:38:51,037 --> 00:38:52,705
Oh , I don 't think that 's so revealing .

600
00:38:52,872 --> 00:38:55,416
But who is Judd ? A psychiatrist .

601
00:38:55,583 --> 00:38:57,627
Now , it 's quite natural that he should read books

602
00:38:57,794 --> 00:38:59,879
on the history of old religious societies .

603
00:39:00,046 --> 00:39:02,465
But why should Mrs. Redi , a woman with a beauty parlor ?

604
00:39:02,632 --> 00:39:04,676
- I don 't know . - That 's just it .

605
00:39:04,843 --> 00:39:06,803
And this figure . She traced it .

606
00:39:07,595 --> 00:39:10,056
The book I saw at the library had been marked " perfect "

607
00:39:10,223 --> 00:39:12,267
by the library inspector in March .

608
00:39:12,433 --> 00:39:14,018
Mrs. Redi had it out in April ,

609
00:39:14,185 --> 00:39:15,979
and no one else had read it since .

610
00:39:16,145 --> 00:39:18,398
This figure is the symbol of the Palladists .

611
00:39:19,065 --> 00:39:21,818
It 's all clear to me now . So clear .

612
00:39:21,985 --> 00:39:23,736
I thought it would be , but just to be sure ,

613
00:39:23,903 --> 00:39:26,739
I 'll tell you that the Palladists are a society of devil worshipers .

614
00:39:26,906 --> 00:39:27,991
Devil worshipers !

615
00:39:28,658 --> 00:39:30,535
But , look , I 'm serious .

616
00:39:30,702 --> 00:39:32,495
It 's a very real and earnest society .

617
00:39:32,662 --> 00:39:34,831
- A dangerous society . - I can imagine .

618
00:39:34,998 --> 00:39:37,709
Well , sometime before those nice white gloves are dry ,

619
00:39:37,876 --> 00:39:40,670
you 're going to go and find out a few things about this Mrs. Redi .

620
00:39:41,462 --> 00:39:43,715
Is Mrs. Redi nice to work for ?

621
00:39:44,215 --> 00:39:45,758
Uh , Redi 's all right ,

622
00:39:46,259 --> 00:39:48,511
but there 's only one Miss Jacqueline .

623
00:39:48,678 --> 00:39:50,763
Mrs. Redi seems rather an odd woman to me .

624
00:39:50,930 --> 00:39:52,974
She 's really a pretty good sort .

625
00:39:53,141 --> 00:39:55,602
What does she do with herself after business hours ?

626
00:39:56,728 --> 00:40:00,440
It 's always seemed to me that she was sort of lonely and unhappy .

627
00:40:00,607 --> 00:40:02,525
Well , Mary , I guess most people are .

628
00:40:03,651 --> 00:40:04,903
There . That 's it .

629
00:40:11,034 --> 00:40:13,244
In the old days , this would have been on the house .

630
00:40:14,954 --> 00:40:16,289
Aw , the tip is , anyhow .

631
00:40:16,456 --> 00:40:17,999
Besides , I like to do your hair .

632
00:40:18,166 --> 00:40:19,042
Thank you .

633
00:40:20,752 --> 00:40:22,587
Do you know what this is , Frances ?

634
00:40:23,212 --> 00:40:24,464
Why , I ought to .

635
00:40:25,882 --> 00:40:27,592
It 's Mrs. Redi 's new trademark .

636
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:29,969
Of course . I should have known .

637
00:40:30,720 --> 00:40:32,472
This figure 's been puzzling me .

638
00:40:41,606 --> 00:40:43,733
Hello , Mary . It 's nice to see you .

639
00:40:43,900 --> 00:40:45,902
- No news of Jacqueline ? - I 'm afraid not .

640
00:40:46,069 --> 00:40:47,153
Well , that 's too bad .

641
00:40:54,369 --> 00:40:55,787
What did she want ?

642
00:40:55,954 --> 00:40:57,705
Nothing . I just did her hair .

643
00:40:57,872 --> 00:40:59,457
What were you talking about ?

644
00:40:59,624 --> 00:41:00,541
Nothing .

645
00:41:01,042 --> 00:41:03,920
Nothing ? Why , that 's absurd .

646
00:41:04,087 --> 00:41:06,965
I heard you laughing and talking . She was asking questions .

647
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:09,133
Oh , well , she was asking about you .

648
00:41:09,300 --> 00:41:11,678
Whether it was nice to work for you or not .

649
00:41:11,844 --> 00:41:12,887
And that was all ?

650
00:41:13,930 --> 00:41:16,057
Well , she asked about the trademark .

651
00:41:16,683 --> 00:41:19,310
- What did she want to know ? - She showed me a drawing .

652
00:41:19,477 --> 00:41:23,022
Oh , you fool ! Why , that symbol is us .

653
00:41:23,564 --> 00:41:24,482
Us !

654
00:41:25,233 --> 00:41:27,110
She was asking about us !

655
00:41:49,882 --> 00:41:52,135
- Mary - Yes ? -

656
00:41:52,301 --> 00:41:53,886
This is Mrs. Redi , Mary .

657
00:41:54,637 --> 00:41:56,180
Oh , I 'll be out in a minute .

658
00:41:56,347 --> 00:41:57,890
That won 't be necessary .

659
00:41:58,057 --> 00:41:59,475
I haven 't much to say .

660
00:42:01,227 --> 00:42:04,022
If I were you , Mary , I 'd go back to school .

661
00:42:04,564 --> 00:42:07,400
I 'd make no further attempt to find Jacqueline .

662
00:42:07,859 --> 00:42:10,194
I can 't give up looking for her , Mrs. Redi ,

663
00:42:10,361 --> 00:42:11,738
no matter what you 're hinting at .

664
00:42:11,904 --> 00:42:14,532
I have no intention whatsoever of hinting .

665
00:42:15,658 --> 00:42:18,327
Your sister , Mary , is a murderess .

666
00:42:19,078 --> 00:42:20,955
She killed Irving August .

667
00:42:21,539 --> 00:42:22,915
Stabbed him out of fright

668
00:42:23,082 --> 00:42:25,043
when he discovered where she was hiding .

669
00:42:26,252 --> 00:42:27,795
I don 't believe you .

670
00:42:27,962 --> 00:42:30,173
I had to help get rid of the body .

671
00:42:31,007 --> 00:42:32,759
You saw it on the subway .

672
00:42:33,718 --> 00:42:36,220
And I warn you , Mary , go back .

673
00:42:37,305 --> 00:42:38,723
You don 't know what you 're doing

674
00:42:38,890 --> 00:42:40,725
or what dreadful things you might bring about

675
00:42:40,892 --> 00:42:42,101
by looking for your sister .

676
00:42:43,269 --> 00:42:45,063
You go back to school .

677
00:42:57,742 --> 00:43:00,745
- I 'm sorry to be late , Natalie . - We haven 't begun tea yet .

678
00:43:05,291 --> 00:43:07,335
- Hello , Frances . - Hello , Mrs. Redi .

679
00:43:08,836 --> 00:43:10,963
- How do you do ? - Mrs. Redi .

680
00:43:13,132 --> 00:43:14,258
Won 't you pour ?

681
00:43:18,221 --> 00:43:19,806
I 'm sorry . I 'm nervous .

682
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:22,391
- This is very trying for me . - I know .

683
00:43:22,558 --> 00:43:24,102
You introduced Jacqueline to us .

684
00:43:24,268 --> 00:43:26,521
- But how could you tell ? - I should have known .

685
00:43:26,687 --> 00:43:29,148
She had no sincerity , no real belief .

686
00:43:29,315 --> 00:43:31,067
Miss Rowan , do you take cream ?

687
00:43:31,609 --> 00:43:33,736
Please , Natalie , would you mind pouring ?

688
00:43:34,570 --> 00:43:36,197
You shouldn 't be nervous .

689
00:43:36,364 --> 00:43:39,534
There 's nothing personal or vengeful in what we are about to do .

690
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:41,452
We have only to make a decision .

691
00:43:41,619 --> 00:43:44,372
But it can be such a horrible decision ,

692
00:43:45,039 --> 00:43:47,458
because we 're all pledged to nonviolence .

693
00:43:47,834 --> 00:43:48,709
Now , this - -

694
00:43:48,876 --> 00:43:50,211
Our founder must have known

695
00:43:50,378 --> 00:43:53,214
when he wrote these seemingly contradictory rules .

696
00:43:54,048 --> 00:43:56,217
The rule of nonviolence

697
00:43:56,384 --> 00:43:59,303
and the law that whoever betrays us must die .

698
00:43:59,887 --> 00:44:00,888
He must have known .

699
00:44:01,055 --> 00:44:02,682
But I don 't understand it .

700
00:44:02,849 --> 00:44:05,685
Some of us , Frances , must believe without understanding .

701
00:44:06,936 --> 00:44:08,229
Yes , I suppose so .

702
00:44:08,396 --> 00:44:10,940
I went back through the history last night .

703
00:44:11,107 --> 00:44:13,359
I read about Johann Rosenquartz .

704
00:44:13,901 --> 00:44:17,029
- I read what he wrote about - - - I can quote it fully , Mrs. Redi .

705
00:44:17,488 --> 00:44:20,283
" We will avoid violence . For , once undertaken ,

706
00:44:20,449 --> 00:44:22,535
violence can become its own master

707
00:44:22,702 --> 00:44:24,287
and lead to either good or evil . "

708
00:44:24,453 --> 00:44:26,789
- But he also wrote that - - - I can quote that too .

709
00:44:28,708 --> 00:44:31,878
" Those who go out into the marketplaces and let their tongues speak of us

710
00:44:32,044 --> 00:44:34,255
and give knowledge of our being and our deeds ,

711
00:44:34,422 --> 00:44:36,465
whomsoever doeth this shall die . "

712
00:44:36,632 --> 00:44:37,842
I 'm puzzled .

713
00:44:38,176 --> 00:44:42,305
Since our order was founded , six betrayals have been listed .

714
00:44:42,471 --> 00:44:44,348
And six deaths as punishment .

715
00:44:45,308 --> 00:44:47,351
- And now there 's Jacqueline . - Oh , but ...

716
00:44:48,394 --> 00:44:50,229
But you can 't do anything to her .

717
00:44:51,022 --> 00:44:53,900
- You mustn 't hurt her ! - But she betrayed us , Frances .

718
00:44:54,066 --> 00:44:57,361
She didn 't betray us . She was only going to a doctor .

719
00:44:57,528 --> 00:44:58,529
A psychiatrist .

720
00:44:58,696 --> 00:45:00,865
She told him , Frances . She told him about us .

721
00:45:01,032 --> 00:45:02,617
I know this is difficult for you .

722
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:05,077
- I know that you love her . - But she didn 't betray us !

723
00:45:05,244 --> 00:45:06,412
Even if I believed that ,

724
00:45:06,579 --> 00:45:08,873
I would still consider her a very dangerous woman .

725
00:45:09,040 --> 00:45:11,417
There is the matter of Irving August 's death .

726
00:45:12,418 --> 00:45:14,837
Without consulting me , Mrs. Redi was " I advised enough

727
00:45:15,004 --> 00:45:17,173
to have the body removed by Leo and Durk .

728
00:45:18,591 --> 00:45:20,343
This makes us all a party to the crime .

729
00:45:21,761 --> 00:45:23,095
What if there 's a trial ?

730
00:45:23,930 --> 00:45:26,933
What if Jacqueline is asked about the removal of the body ?

731
00:45:28,059 --> 00:45:30,519
Do you think , Frances , that she would keep silent ?

732
00:45:30,978 --> 00:45:34,315
It is a real danger and one which forces our decision .

733
00:45:34,899 --> 00:45:37,818
- And Jacqueline 's sister ? - I 've taken care of Mary .

734
00:45:38,361 --> 00:45:40,863
I 've spoken to her , and she 's going back to school .

735
00:45:41,030 --> 00:45:43,741
Good . Then it is decided .

736
00:45:44,408 --> 00:45:46,994
Leo and Durk and I will complete our plans .

737
00:46:01,592 --> 00:46:02,635
Mary !

738
00:46:08,474 --> 00:46:11,686
This is wonderful , your coming here so unexpectedly .

739
00:46:12,311 --> 00:46:14,146
It 's almost like a wish come true .

740
00:46:15,940 --> 00:46:17,441
I want to show you my room .

741
00:46:18,567 --> 00:46:20,027
I want you to see all of it .

742
00:46:20,820 --> 00:46:22,613
But it 's a small room , Jason .

743
00:46:22,780 --> 00:46:24,615
It 's grown big with the years .

744
00:46:25,574 --> 00:46:28,411
And my window , through which I see the world .

745
00:46:29,203 --> 00:46:30,746
It 's beautiful .

746
00:46:30,913 --> 00:46:33,499
That searchlight and the stars .

747
00:46:33,666 --> 00:46:35,293
Oh , that 's not a searchlight .

748
00:46:35,459 --> 00:46:38,421
It 's a sword blade cutting the blue cloak of a prince .

749
00:46:39,005 --> 00:46:40,715
- Not stars - - - Jason .

750
00:46:41,299 --> 00:46:43,259
I 'm going back to Highcliffe .

751
00:46:43,718 --> 00:46:45,011
I 've come to say goodbye .

752
00:46:45,803 --> 00:46:49,557
But I thought your coming up here to the third floor to see me ...

753
00:46:50,433 --> 00:46:52,643
well , that it was your advent into my world .

754
00:46:53,436 --> 00:46:54,770
Turns out to be goodbye . Why ?

755
00:46:55,396 --> 00:46:57,273
Please don 't make me tell you , Jason .

756
00:46:57,732 --> 00:46:59,984
I thought I was your friend , Mary .

757
00:47:00,151 --> 00:47:02,236
Just " goodbye " isn 't enough for a friend .

758
00:47:05,948 --> 00:47:07,283
I 'd begun to write again .

759
00:47:08,242 --> 00:47:10,244
That 's what I was doing when you came in .

760
00:47:11,495 --> 00:47:13,039
It 's because of Jacqueline .

761
00:47:14,081 --> 00:47:15,833
I can 't go on looking for her .

762
00:47:16,876 --> 00:47:18,294
You went to see Mrs. Redi .

763
00:47:18,794 --> 00:47:20,629
She told you something . What was it ?

764
00:47:21,630 --> 00:47:23,257
Jacqueline 's a murderess .

765
00:47:24,050 --> 00:47:25,676
She killed a man .

766
00:47:26,218 --> 00:47:27,178
You believe that ?

767
00:47:27,845 --> 00:47:30,639
I have to . It was Irving August .

768
00:47:31,140 --> 00:47:34,727
Everything Mrs. Redi said , it fits in with what I saw .

769
00:47:35,227 --> 00:47:38,606
She even knew that I 'd seen his body on the subway .

770
00:47:38,773 --> 00:47:41,233
But if it 's true , then there 's all the more reason

771
00:47:41,400 --> 00:47:42,735
for you to find Jacqueline .

772
00:47:43,277 --> 00:47:46,489
And Gregory , he loves her .

773
00:47:47,490 --> 00:47:50,701
He loves you , Mary . You 'll have to tell him .

774
00:47:50,868 --> 00:47:53,788
He 's Jacqueline 's husband . I can 't .

775
00:47:53,954 --> 00:47:55,873
But you 've got to tell him , Mary .

776
00:47:56,040 --> 00:47:58,376
Even if only for the practical reason that he 's a lawyer

777
00:47:58,542 --> 00:47:59,752
and will know what to do .

778
00:48:00,461 --> 00:48:01,629
I 'm going to phone him .

779
00:48:07,051 --> 00:48:08,636
Well , she 's got to be found .

780
00:48:09,553 --> 00:48:10,805
That 's the first step .

781
00:48:11,972 --> 00:48:14,725
She 's got to be found so she can give herself up to the police .

782
00:48:14,892 --> 00:48:16,644
But we 've tried so long to find her .

783
00:48:17,395 --> 00:48:19,021
Judd could tell us , if he would .

784
00:48:19,688 --> 00:48:22,400
- Do you think he knows about this ? - I don 't know .

785
00:48:23,317 --> 00:48:24,568
Well , he 's clever .

786
00:48:24,735 --> 00:48:26,195
And he 's cautious , in his way .

787
00:48:26,737 --> 00:48:29,281
I think if he knew , he 'd advise her to do what I want .

788
00:48:29,448 --> 00:48:31,784
Surrender herself to the police and stand trial .

789
00:48:33,244 --> 00:48:35,704
- I don 't think he knows . - We could tell him .

790
00:48:38,249 --> 00:48:40,876
- Could you find him ? - I suppose so .

791
00:48:41,919 --> 00:48:43,879
I guess I could pick him up somewhere .

792
00:48:44,046 --> 00:48:47,174
Jason . I sometimes wonder ...

793
00:48:47,842 --> 00:48:51,470
You 're so sweet to me . So kind and sympathetic .

794
00:48:52,388 --> 00:48:54,306
I don 't know how I can ever thank you .

795
00:48:54,807 --> 00:48:55,766
Thank me ?

796
00:48:56,684 --> 00:48:58,269
You don 't have to thank me .

797
00:49:04,733 --> 00:49:05,818
What 's that ?

798
00:49:06,277 --> 00:49:08,571
Verse . Verse I wrote .

799
00:50:22,436 --> 00:50:23,729
Don 't bother going up .

800
00:50:23,896 --> 00:50:26,065
I can do this all night , Jason . Watch .

801
00:50:36,450 --> 00:50:38,327
Following me to find Jacqueline ?

802
00:50:38,494 --> 00:50:40,579
- Mm-hm . - Well , it won 't work .

803
00:50:41,121 --> 00:50:43,290
Love and understanding won 't make a good detective

804
00:50:43,457 --> 00:50:44,959
out of a recalcitrant poet .

805
00:50:45,125 --> 00:50:47,628
Actually , there are two favors I want to ask of you .

806
00:50:47,795 --> 00:50:50,130
One as a poet , one as a detective .

807
00:50:50,881 --> 00:50:53,676
Sounds strange . I 'm going to be very wary .

808
00:50:53,842 --> 00:50:56,178
Some time ago , you spoke about my writing again .

809
00:50:56,845 --> 00:50:58,222
I want your help .

810
00:50:58,389 --> 00:51:00,349
I 'd like you to bring this to your publisher .

811
00:51:02,560 --> 00:51:04,103
This is curious , Jason .

812
00:51:04,812 --> 00:51:08,357
Half the time you talk as if Shakespeare weren 't fit to tie your Shoelaces .

813
00:51:08,524 --> 00:51:10,359
Now this sudden humility .

814
00:51:10,526 --> 00:51:12,903
I should like people to read what I have written .

815
00:51:13,320 --> 00:51:15,823
I hope it 'll find as much favor as your other book .

816
00:51:15,990 --> 00:51:19,076
But somehow I doubt it . The time is out of tune .

817
00:51:19,243 --> 00:51:21,120
Why not let your publisher judge that ?

818
00:51:22,288 --> 00:51:25,207
Wait . There 's that other favor .

819
00:51:25,374 --> 00:51:26,458
I 'd forgotten .

820
00:51:26,625 --> 00:51:28,877
Tell me where Jacqueline is . We 've got to find her .

821
00:51:29,044 --> 00:51:31,130
You don 't really expect me to do that , do you ?

822
00:51:31,297 --> 00:51:33,841
- Yes , when I tell you . - Tell me what ?

823
00:51:34,008 --> 00:51:36,510
You 'll have good enough sense to tell us where she is

824
00:51:36,677 --> 00:51:38,137
when I tell you she 's a murderess .

825
00:51:38,304 --> 00:51:39,221
She killed a man .

826
00:51:45,185 --> 00:51:48,272
Tell me , why this sudden desire to publish ?

827
00:51:48,439 --> 00:51:50,941
To awaken like Byron and find yourself famous ?

828
00:51:51,108 --> 00:51:53,360
- I think it 's time . - No other reason ?

829
00:51:53,944 --> 00:51:56,947
No woman ? Not the little Miss Gibson ?

830
00:51:57,114 --> 00:51:57,865
Perhaps .

831
00:52:05,164 --> 00:52:06,665
Wait a minute . I 'll call her .

832
00:52:10,044 --> 00:52:11,629
Jacqueline , this is Judd .

833
00:52:16,884 --> 00:52:17,926
Jacqueline .

834
00:52:20,012 --> 00:52:23,390
- Who is it ? - Judd . I 'm here with your sister .

835
00:52:23,557 --> 00:52:24,475
Come on down .

836
00:52:41,575 --> 00:52:42,951
Oh , Mary .

837
00:52:44,453 --> 00:52:45,579
Jacqueline .

838
00:52:49,333 --> 00:52:50,250
It 's all right .

839
00:52:51,251 --> 00:52:53,379
You 're safe . Nothing 's going to hurt you .

840
00:52:53,545 --> 00:52:55,506
Your husband seems very certain of that .

841
00:52:55,673 --> 00:52:59,343
Yes . I 'm very certain there 's only one way to help you , Jacqueline .

842
00:52:59,885 --> 00:53:00,928
To protect you .

843
00:53:01,553 --> 00:53:03,013
You 've got to come with us .

844
00:53:03,180 --> 00:53:06,392
Let me do all I can as a lawyer to straighten out Irving August 's death .

845
00:53:06,558 --> 00:53:08,352
You must come with us , darling .

846
00:53:08,519 --> 00:53:09,770
Let us help you .

847
00:53:27,663 --> 00:53:30,791
For me , this seems to be the end of a delightful relationship .

848
00:53:34,420 --> 00:53:36,755
Here , this will put some life into you .

849
00:53:38,549 --> 00:53:40,384
It 's like coming back to life .

850
00:53:41,719 --> 00:53:45,097
It would be much easier , Jacqueline , if you 'd tell me exactly what happened .

851
00:53:45,264 --> 00:53:46,598
I 'd know what to do for you .

852
00:53:47,266 --> 00:53:48,475
Please , Jacqueline .

853
00:53:52,813 --> 00:53:54,398
You know about the Palladists .

854
00:53:55,983 --> 00:53:57,109
You know who they are .

855
00:53:58,152 --> 00:53:59,278
What they are .

856
00:54:01,238 --> 00:54:02,156
I was one of them .

857
00:54:03,115 --> 00:54:05,617
Jacqueline was always a sensationalist ,

858
00:54:05,784 --> 00:54:07,870
trying to seize on to something ,

859
00:54:09,413 --> 00:54:11,039
anything to bring her happiness .

860
00:54:12,374 --> 00:54:15,335
Through Mrs. Redi , she stumbled onto the Palladist movement .

861
00:54:16,378 --> 00:54:17,463
It appealed to her .

862
00:54:18,046 --> 00:54:19,590
I wasn 't happy with them .

863
00:54:21,550 --> 00:54:22,718
Wanted to break away .

864
00:54:24,386 --> 00:54:25,429
I was miserable .

865
00:54:27,556 --> 00:54:28,974
I went to Louis for help .

866
00:54:30,851 --> 00:54:32,519
They felt that I 'd betrayed them .

867
00:54:34,521 --> 00:54:35,731
They wanted me to die .

868
00:54:37,399 --> 00:54:38,567
Kill myself .

869
00:54:40,903 --> 00:54:42,863
They kept me locked up at La Sagesse .

870
00:54:44,531 --> 00:54:46,033
I was there such a long time .

871
00:54:47,075 --> 00:54:49,912
You can imagine the effect of such imprisonment on Jacqueline .

872
00:54:50,078 --> 00:54:51,163
I was terrified .

873
00:54:53,582 --> 00:54:55,501
Darkness in the corners of the room .

874
00:54:57,044 --> 00:54:58,462
All the little noises .

875
00:55:00,589 --> 00:55:02,257
Then one night , the door opened .

876
00:55:04,092 --> 00:55:05,177
A man came in .

877
00:55:06,720 --> 00:55:07,805
Tiptoeing in .

878
00:55:09,640 --> 00:55:11,141
I had a scissors in my hand .

879
00:55:12,434 --> 00:55:13,560
I struck at him .

880
00:55:13,977 --> 00:55:17,022
Don 't . We know what happened . Don 't go on .

881
00:55:17,189 --> 00:55:19,149
Any court in the land would understand .

882
00:55:20,067 --> 00:55:22,444
We 'll wait a few days . Let you rest .

883
00:55:23,070 --> 00:55:24,321
Then we 'll go to the police .

884
00:55:24,905 --> 00:55:27,908
Why can 't Jacqueline stay here with me for a few days ?

885
00:55:28,075 --> 00:55:29,493
You 'd like that , wouldn 't you ?

886
00:55:31,078 --> 00:55:32,579
There 's my old friend .

887
00:55:33,997 --> 00:55:37,543
- The searchlight ? - Mm-hm . Cyrano 's sword .

888
00:55:37,709 --> 00:55:39,628
That 's a funny thing to call it .

889
00:55:39,795 --> 00:55:40,754
I like it .

890
00:55:41,380 --> 00:55:43,006
I 've always loved the story .

891
00:55:43,841 --> 00:55:46,593
A man knowing he couldn 't have the woman he loved

892
00:55:46,760 --> 00:55:48,637
and wooing her for his friend .

893
00:55:50,264 --> 00:55:51,849
We 're friends , aren 't we , Gregory ?

894
00:55:53,016 --> 00:55:55,102
It 's been a hard evening for both of you .

895
00:55:55,477 --> 00:55:57,938
Perhaps you ought to take Jacqueline to your room , Mary .

896
00:56:05,529 --> 00:56:06,655
Good night , Jacqueline .

897
00:56:09,867 --> 00:56:11,785
- Good night , Mary . - Good night .

898
00:56:15,706 --> 00:56:17,541
This is no time to play Cyrano .

899
00:56:18,417 --> 00:56:19,793
What was in your mind ?

900
00:56:19,960 --> 00:56:22,045
I wanted to get things clear for Jacqueline .

901
00:56:22,212 --> 00:56:24,256
- To let her know . - To let her know what ?

902
00:56:24,798 --> 00:56:26,049
That you love Mary .

903
00:56:27,050 --> 00:56:28,844
She 'll have to know sometime .

904
00:56:29,011 --> 00:56:29,845
Not from me .

905
00:56:31,221 --> 00:56:32,306
And not from Mary .

906
00:56:39,897 --> 00:56:42,190
Goodbye , darling . I 'll only be gone until 3 .

907
00:56:42,357 --> 00:56:43,275
Goodbye .

908
00:56:43,442 --> 00:56:45,694
If you get lonely , go down and see Mrs. Romari .

909
00:56:45,861 --> 00:56:47,613
I told her you were staying with me .

910
00:56:51,325 --> 00:56:52,451
I won 't be lonely .

911
00:57:02,044 --> 00:57:06,131
♪ " When Will you pay me ? " ♪

912
00:57:06,298 --> 00:57:11,511
♪ Say the bells of Old Bailey ♪

913
00:57:11,678 --> 00:57:15,390
♪ " That I don 't know " ♪

914
00:57:15,557 --> 00:57:19,770
♪ Says the great bell of Bow ♪

915
00:57:21,897 --> 00:57:25,275
♪ Here comes a candle To light you to bed ♪

916
00:57:25,442 --> 00:57:29,905
♪ Here comes a chopper To chop off your head ♪

917
00:57:31,531 --> 00:57:33,075
Yes , this is Mary .

918
00:57:35,535 --> 00:57:37,162
But she couldn 't have gone out .

919
00:57:38,664 --> 00:57:39,623
No .

920
00:57:40,707 --> 00:57:44,294
Are you sure it wasn 't Jason she went with , or Mr. Ward ?

921
00:57:45,754 --> 00:57:46,755
Two men ?

922
00:57:48,548 --> 00:57:49,591
No .

923
00:57:51,343 --> 00:57:53,595
I 'll get home as soon as I can , Mr. Romari .

924
00:57:54,429 --> 00:57:56,807
The acceptance of a secret is an obligation .

925
00:57:57,391 --> 00:57:59,351
In this case , my dear , the obligation carried with it

926
00:57:59,518 --> 00:58:01,645
the necessity of dying if one betrayed that secret .

927
00:58:01,812 --> 00:58:03,146
You understand that , don 't you ?

928
00:58:04,523 --> 00:58:07,150
Yes , I understand it .

929
00:58:07,567 --> 00:58:09,736
Then you also understand that you must die .

930
00:58:10,779 --> 00:58:11,655
No .

931
00:58:12,322 --> 00:58:14,574
Jacqueline , you 've spoken so often of ending it all .

932
00:58:14,741 --> 00:58:17,828
I can 't understand why this should be so difficult for you .

933
00:58:18,286 --> 00:58:19,871
You have only to drink a little .

934
00:58:20,038 --> 00:58:21,373
Yes , Jacqueline .

935
00:58:21,540 --> 00:58:23,250
You were always talking suicide ,

936
00:58:23,417 --> 00:58:25,585
of ending your life when you wanted to .

937
00:58:26,586 --> 00:58:27,629
Yes .

938
00:58:28,672 --> 00:58:29,881
When I wanted to .

939
00:58:30,048 --> 00:58:31,008
It doesn 't matter .

940
00:58:31,591 --> 00:58:33,593
You want to now . You should want to .

941
00:58:33,760 --> 00:58:35,220
It is your obligation , your duty .

942
00:58:35,387 --> 00:58:37,264
You have only to stretch out your hand ,

943
00:58:37,431 --> 00:58:39,307
take up the glass and drink a little .

944
00:58:39,766 --> 00:58:40,976
It won 't hurt .

945
00:58:41,727 --> 00:58:43,729
No , no , no .

946
00:58:45,063 --> 00:58:47,691
You have a strange kind of courage , Jason .

947
00:58:49,568 --> 00:58:50,944
Perhaps you have enough courage

948
00:58:51,111 --> 00:58:53,572
to hear what I have been keeping from you all these years .

949
00:58:53,739 --> 00:58:57,951
That girl you loved , that other patient of mine ...

950
00:58:58,744 --> 00:59:00,078
she didn 't disappear .

951
00:59:00,912 --> 00:59:02,122
She 's in an asylum .

952
00:59:02,622 --> 00:59:04,416
A horrible , raving thing .

953
00:59:06,293 --> 00:59:07,669
I never wanted you to know .

954
00:59:09,463 --> 00:59:10,589
And all the while ...

955
00:59:11,882 --> 00:59:13,216
you 've been my friend .

956
00:59:24,770 --> 00:59:28,148
Please , may I have a drink of water ?

957
00:59:29,191 --> 00:59:30,525
I 'm very thirsty .

958
00:59:31,651 --> 00:59:32,694
Drink .

959
00:59:33,653 --> 00:59:34,529
No .

960
00:59:35,197 --> 00:59:37,699
There will be no water and no rest . You may as we " drink .

961
00:59:45,040 --> 00:59:46,500
No ! No !

962
00:59:50,462 --> 00:59:52,255
If you like , I 'll go with you to dinner .

963
00:59:52,422 --> 00:59:54,007
- I 'd like that . - Jason !

964
00:59:55,383 --> 00:59:56,635
I can 't find Gregory .

965
00:59:56,802 --> 00:59:58,178
I 've been trying to find him .

966
00:59:58,345 --> 00:59:59,721
What 's wrong , Mary ?

967
00:59:59,888 --> 01:00:02,015
Jacqueline . Mr. Romari phoned me .

968
01:00:02,182 --> 01:00:05,268
She went out this afternoon with two men he 'd never seen before .

969
01:00:05,435 --> 01:00:07,187
They may have been friends of hers .

970
01:00:07,354 --> 01:00:10,065
No , she wouldn 't have gone with anyone unless she were compelled .

971
01:00:10,232 --> 01:00:13,527
All these months of hiding have made her frightened of the streets and people .

972
01:00:14,778 --> 01:00:16,863
- I wonder ... - What ?

973
01:00:17,614 --> 01:00:19,032
They may have found her .

974
01:00:19,491 --> 01:00:20,700
Would they hurt her ?

975
01:00:21,576 --> 01:00:22,536
I don 't know .

976
01:00:23,703 --> 01:00:26,081
You 'd better go up to your room and wait for us , Mary .

977
01:00:32,420 --> 01:00:33,713
Go ahead , Jacqueline .

978
01:00:35,507 --> 01:00:36,466
Go ahead .

979
01:00:41,763 --> 01:00:42,848
It is late .

980
01:00:44,933 --> 01:00:46,309
Drink it , Jacqueline !

981
01:00:46,476 --> 01:00:48,228
There 's nothing else for you to do !

982
01:00:48,395 --> 01:00:49,771
They say you 've got to die .

983
01:00:50,313 --> 01:00:54,151
Drink it , Jacqueline ! You 've got to ! I can 't stand this !

984
01:01:07,330 --> 01:01:10,542
No ! No , I can 't let you die !

985
01:01:10,709 --> 01:01:15,255
The only time I was ever happy was when I was working with you .

986
01:01:16,631 --> 01:01:19,217
You were always so good to me .

987
01:01:38,320 --> 01:01:41,573
You may go now , Jacqueline . The decision was against violence .

988
01:01:41,740 --> 01:01:43,283
But there 'll be another decision .

989
01:01:43,700 --> 01:01:46,995
Today , tomorrow ... We 'll find you .

990
01:01:47,162 --> 01:01:48,205
But now you may go .

991
01:01:53,376 --> 01:01:54,920
I told you you could go .

992
01:05:18,665 --> 01:05:20,875
Please help me . There 's a man following me .

993
01:05:21,042 --> 01:05:22,293
I shouldn 't wonder , babe .

994
01:05:22,460 --> 01:05:23,670
Please , I 'm serious . Help me .

995
01:05:23,837 --> 01:05:25,713
I 'll help you to a beer and a sandwich .

996
01:05:25,880 --> 01:05:27,340
Come along , babe . Come along .

997
01:06:34,407 --> 01:06:35,700
Who are you ?

998
01:06:36,743 --> 01:06:37,827
I 'm Mimi .

999
01:06:38,578 --> 01:06:40,038
- I 'm dying . - No .

1000
01:06:40,538 --> 01:06:43,249
Yes . I 've been quiet .

1001
01:06:44,125 --> 01:06:45,585
Oh , ever so quiet .

1002
01:06:46,127 --> 01:06:47,545
I hardly move ,

1003
01:06:48,171 --> 01:06:50,381
and yet it keeps coming all the time ,

1004
01:06:50,548 --> 01:06:51,966
closer and closer .

1005
01:06:52,634 --> 01:06:56,804
And I rest and I rest and ... still I 'm dying .

1006
01:06:57,555 --> 01:06:59,057
And you don 't want to die .

1007
01:07:00,391 --> 01:07:01,851
I 've always wanted to die .

1008
01:07:02,894 --> 01:07:05,522
- Always . - I 'm afraid .

1009
01:07:07,482 --> 01:07:10,777
And I 'm tired of being afraid , of waiting .

1010
01:07:11,736 --> 01:07:14,322
- Why wait ? - I 'm not going to wait .

1011
01:07:15,031 --> 01:07:17,909
I 'm going out , and I 'm going to laugh and dance

1012
01:07:18,076 --> 01:07:20,495
and do all the things I used to do .

1013
01:07:20,662 --> 01:07:21,663
And then ?

1014
01:07:22,622 --> 01:07:23,706
I don 't know .

1015
01:07:26,834 --> 01:07:27,961
You will die .

1016
01:07:48,648 --> 01:07:50,858
Now that you 've hounded and worried her half to death ,

1017
01:07:51,025 --> 01:07:52,402
you don 't even know where she is .

1018
01:07:54,153 --> 01:07:55,989
At least tell me , has she been here ?

1019
01:07:56,155 --> 01:07:57,156
Yes .

1020
01:07:57,323 --> 01:07:59,033
She left here an hour ago .

1021
01:07:59,200 --> 01:08:01,828
She may even be home by now . Why don 't you try it ?

1022
01:08:02,495 --> 01:08:03,538
All right , Jason .

1023
01:08:12,213 --> 01:08:13,506
The devil worshipers .

1024
01:08:14,382 --> 01:08:16,009
The lovers of evil .

1025
01:08:17,427 --> 01:08:18,511
It 's a joke .

1026
01:08:19,220 --> 01:08:20,555
A pathetic little joke .

1027
01:08:20,722 --> 01:08:22,682
We haven 't asked your opinion .

1028
01:08:23,224 --> 01:08:24,976
I propose to give it to you anyway .

1029
01:08:26,102 --> 01:08:28,438
You 're a poor , wretched group of people who have ...

1030
01:08:29,230 --> 01:08:30,732
taken the wrong turning .

1031
01:08:31,232 --> 01:08:32,191
Wrong ?

1032
01:08:35,361 --> 01:08:37,363
Who knows what is wrong or right ?

1033
01:08:38,698 --> 01:08:41,117
If I prefer to believe in satanic majesty and power ,

1034
01:08:41,284 --> 01:08:42,368
who can deny me ?

1035
01:08:43,620 --> 01:08:46,456
What proof can you bring that good is superior to evil ?

1036
01:08:47,665 --> 01:08:49,250
It 's hard to put into words .

1037
01:08:49,751 --> 01:08:50,668
But you 're wrong .

1038
01:08:50,835 --> 01:08:52,170
One proof .

1039
01:08:53,171 --> 01:08:54,505
I 'll prove you wrong .

1040
01:08:54,672 --> 01:08:57,133
This afternoon , Jason and I were talking together ,

1041
01:08:57,800 --> 01:09:00,553
and I remembered certain phrases from childhood .

1042
01:09:01,095 --> 01:09:03,097
Simple , half-forgotten words .

1043
01:09:03,681 --> 01:09:05,058
It was the Lord 's Prayer .

1044
01:09:05,933 --> 01:09:09,937
I 'm a physician , yet not I nor any of my colleagues ,

1045
01:09:10,104 --> 01:09:11,356
no matter how learned ,

1046
01:09:12,148 --> 01:09:14,525
ever found a substitute for those few words

1047
01:09:14,692 --> 01:09:16,527
as a rule for human relationship .

1048
01:09:17,862 --> 01:09:19,113
You might remember them .

1049
01:09:20,031 --> 01:09:21,407
" Forgive us our trespasses ,

1050
01:09:22,408 --> 01:09:24,535
as we forgive those who trespass against us . "

1051
01:09:25,870 --> 01:09:28,665
There 's a sentence for you people from that same prayer .

1052
01:09:29,374 --> 01:09:32,752
" Lead us not into temptation , but deliver us from evil . "

1053
01:09:37,256 --> 01:09:38,925
All right . Thank you very much .

1054
01:09:43,346 --> 01:09:45,306
That was Dr. Judd , Mary .

1055
01:09:45,473 --> 01:09:47,684
He phoned to say Jacqueline 's on her way here .

1056
01:09:49,936 --> 01:09:51,729
- Gregory . - Yes ?

1057
01:09:52,522 --> 01:09:54,857
You 'd better take Jacqueline with you tonight .

1058
01:09:55,024 --> 01:09:56,734
It 's what I should have done yesterday .

1059
01:09:57,402 --> 01:09:59,821
I 'll take her away someplace where she can rest .

1060
01:10:02,073 --> 01:10:03,324
Mary .

1061
01:10:03,491 --> 01:10:05,785
No . Stay nearby . I want to talk to you .

1062
01:10:07,495 --> 01:10:08,538
I love you .

1063
01:10:09,330 --> 01:10:11,833
- You know that ? - Yes .

1064
01:10:14,168 --> 01:10:18,923
I 've never loved anyone before , Gregory , and I do love you .

1065
01:10:19,465 --> 01:10:20,842
You must know that .

1066
01:10:22,176 --> 01:10:23,845
But Jacqueline 's my sister ,

1067
01:10:24,554 --> 01:10:26,973
whom I 'd lost and found again .

1068
01:10:28,599 --> 01:10:29,600
I know .

1069
01:10:30,768 --> 01:10:32,186
I shouldn 't have told you .

1070
01:10:32,353 --> 01:10:33,980
No . I 'm glad .

1071
01:10:35,398 --> 01:10:37,066
At least I 've heard you say it .

1072
01:10:48,161 --> 01:10:49,537
I run to death ,

1073
01:10:50,121 --> 01:10:51,998
and death meets me as fast .

1074
01:10:53,624 --> 01:10:55,960
And all my pleasures are like yesterday .

